From d546dac3473a65eacbeb996f7d574dcf57809d07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:29:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tui): keep command previews readable and expandable

Preserve executable names and exact command copy payloads while sharing
mouse and configured keyboard disclosure state. Enable
unleashed_readable_commands by default; keep legacy rendering on opt-out.

Refs: holdmyspot-com/codex-unleashed#70
Base: openai/codex rust-v0.163.0
(83086188ae0614bd882818ff1aa23f3194962012).
Queue-context prerequisite: the existing patch queue at downstream
64897f4247469148d5ea88261696536e06cef539. The independent upstream
contribution variant includes its own schema and requires no other patches.
The shared schema patch supplies the combined fixture for this queue variant.

TDD: three standalone upstream regressions fail before implementation.
The emitted standalone variant passes just fmt-check and all 18 focused
feature checks on a fresh upstream checkout. Queue integration adds coverage
for grouped historical command presentation alongside collapsed activity.
